QODEKRAFT Learning Platform — Implementation Plan

Overview
A private online learning platform with:

Frontend: React + Vite + Tailwind CSS + PWA
Backend: Python FastAPI + SQLAlchemy + JWT Auth
Database: MySQL
Media Storage: Local filesystem (/media/)
Roles: Admin, Student (RBAC enforced on API)

Architecture
qodekraft-learning-platform/
├── frontend/          # React + Vite + Tailwind + PWA
├── backend/           # FastAPI application
├── media/             # Local file storage
├── docker-compose.yml # Full stack orchestration
├── README.md
└── .env.example

Core modules
- Authentication and role-based access
- Students and approval requests
- Domains and learning access
- Recorded classes
- Assignments and submission review
- Quizzes and results
- Projects and submission review
- Announcements
- Progress and reports
- Platform settings
- PWA installation

Verification Plan
1. Start with docker compose up --build -d.
2. Confirm MySQL is healthy.
3. Confirm backend health endpoint returns healthy.
4. Open the frontend and test admin login.
5. Test student approval and domain assignment.
6. Test recorded classes.
7. Create an assignment, submit it as a student, and review it as admin.
8. Create and attempt a quiz.
9. Submit and review a project.
10. Confirm the QODEKRAFT install control appears inside the top search bar when the browser supports PWA installation.
